        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.083,
            0.882,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "Now, think what would have happened if microorganisms did not exist on Earth?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.133,
            0.43,
            0.153
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A step further"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
            0.18,
            0.247,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.263,
            0.164,
            0.549,
            0.183
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Microbes as a source of biogas"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.187,
            0.86,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": "Many microorganisms, like bacteria and fungi, live in an oxygenfree environment. Some of these bacteria have the ability to decompose plant and animal waste present in the environment or household wastewater. During the process, they release a mixture of gases called biogas primarily composed of carbon dioxide, and a high proportion of another gas, methane. This gas has been used as a fuel source for cooking, heating, generating electricity, and to even run vehicles."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.345,
            0.407,
            0.365
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Be a scientist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.382,
            0.699,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": "Ananda Mohan Chakrabarty (1938–2020) was a scientist who studied bacteria. In 1971, he developed a special bacterium that could break down oil spills, helping to clean the environment. His discovery received a patent in 1980. **Patent** is a copyright given to a person so that no one else can copy, use or sell his/her invention without permission. His work showed how microorganisms could be used to solve environmental problems like pollution. He"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.702,
            0.376,
            0.863,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.505,
            0.248,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.247,
            0.533,
            0.86,
            0.586
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "is remembered for his contributions to science and for protecting the environment using microbes. What are the other problems which you think can be solved with the help of microorganisms?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.599,
            0.869,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "How does the diversity of microorganisms help in our kitchen?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.077,
            0.619,
            0.234,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.627,
            0.582,
            0.647
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2.4.2 Microorganisms and food"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.651,
            0.875,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "Let us try to understand by performing activities in the kitchen."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.078,
            0.717,
            0.237,
            0.733
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "(a) Dough in bowl A"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.077,
            0.737,
            0.237,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
